{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_005 (multiprofile, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, concat) achieved 0.507 accuracy, substantially outperforming config_028 (singleprofile, same encoders, no aggregation) at 0.435, strongly validating the multiprofile+transformer pipeline. Uncertainty: whether the fusion strategy (concat vs. weighted) is a meaningful lever for further improvement in this top-performing architecture. This experiment tests config_010, which is identical to config_005 except fusion changes from concat to weighted—a single-variable perturbation that isolates the fusion effect. If weighted fusion improves accuracy, it opens a family of weighted-fusion multiprofile configurations to exploit in remaining budget; if not, concat is confirmed as the better fusion and we can pivot to testing alternative RNA encoders (scvi_n200, pca_n2000) in the transformer+concat setting. This is the best use of experiment 3 because it is the cheapest informative step: same architecture as config_005 so expected training cost is comparable (~3.5–4.0 GPU hours, slightly less since weighted fusion avoids the dimensionality increase of concat), keeping total spend around ~8.8 GPU hours with 6 experiments still available."
}

